---
layout: tutorial
title: Initialize SDK
description: Add Authentication to a SvelteKit project using AACSearch.
step: 3
---
Before you can use AACSearch, you need to instanciate the AACSearch `Client` class with the project ID and endpoint. 
This tells the SDK where your AACSearch project is hosted and which one to connect to.

The client is then used to initialize services like `Databases` and `Account`, so they all point to the same AACSearch project.

You can do this by instantiating the services you need in a file like `src/lib/aacsearch.js` and **exporting the instances**.

```js
// src/lib/aacsearch.js
import {
  PUBLIC_AACSEARCH_ENDPOINT,
  PUBLIC_AACSEARCH_PROJECT,
} from "$env/static/public";
import { Databases, Account, Client } from "aacsearch";

const client = new Client();
client
  .setEndpoint(PUBLIC_AACSEARCH_ENDPOINT)
  .setProject(PUBLIC_AACSEARCH_PROJECT);

const account = new Account(client);
const tablesDB = new TablesDB(client);

export const aacsearch = {
  client,
  account,
  databases,
};
```

`PUBLIC_AACSEARCH_ENDPOINT` and `PUBLIC_AACSEARCH_PROJECT` are environment variables that are exported in your project's [.env file](https://kit.svelte.dev/docs/modules#$env-dynamic-public).

For example, your `.env` might look something similar to this.

```env
PUBLIC_AACSEARCH_ENDPOINT=https://<REGION>.cloud.aacsearch.io/v1
PUBLIC_AACSEARCH_PROJECT=642sdddf85b440dc7e5bf
```

You can get the values for these variables from the AACSearch console's **Settings** page.